lue, calculating the scaling correctly for each color based on both input and output positions.\n**Proposing shape processing**\n\nI want to rotate the small shape cluster in the task input, aligning the bottom 8-shape with this new orientation. A programmatic approach is better than trying to transcribe ASCII manually. So, I\u2019ll propose using Python code to process the grid.\n\nI'll start by finding the small cluster based on color detection, then look for the connected component excluding colors 8 and 0. I'll compute the scale factor and where to place the rotated small pixels accordingly. Finally, I'll zero out all cells in the 8s region while keeping the top area unchanged. Now, I\u2019ll call a function to implement this!"
