    "arguments": "{\"code\":\"import numpy as np\\n# Copy original grid\\noutput = self.grid.copy()\\n\\n# identify small shape: cells non-zero and not 8\\nsmall_coords = [(x,y) for y in range(self.height) for x in range(self.width)\\n                if self.grid[y,x] != 0 and self.grid[y,x] != 8]\\n# get unique small cluster: they might include extra scattered, but assume single cluster\\n# determine bounding box for small shape\\nxs = [x for x,y in small_coords]\\nys = [y for x,y in small_coords]\\nmin_xs, max_xs = min(xs), max(xs)\\nmin_ys, max_ys = min(ys), max(ys)\\nbw = max_xs - min_xs + 1\\nbh = max_ys - min_ys + 1\\n\\n# find bottom region (8s)\\nlarge_coords = [(x,y) for y in range(self.height) for x in range(self.width) if self.grid[y,x] == 8]\\nlx = [x for x,y in large_coords]\\nly = [y for x,y in large_coords]\\nmin_xl, max_xl = min(lx), max(lx)\\nmin_yl, max_yl = min(ly), max(ly)\\n\\n# scale factor\\nsmall_count = len(small_coords)\\nlarge_count = len(large_coords)\\nscale = int(round(np.sqrt(large_count / small_count)))\\n\\n# clear bottom region\\nfor x,y in large_coords:\\n    output[y,x] = 0\\n\\n# For each small pixel, rotate cw around top-left of small bounding box, then scale and place in bottom region\\nfor (x,y) in small_coords:\\n    C = self.grid[y,x]\\n    dx = x - min_xs\\n    dy = y - min_ys\\n    # rotate 90 deg CW around origin of small bounding box\\n    dx_r = dy\\n    dy_r = (bw - 1) - dx\\n    # scale and place\\n    for i in range(scale):\\n        for j in range(scale):\\n            tx = min_xl + dx_r * scale + i\\n            ty = min_yl + dy_r * scale + j\\n            output[ty, tx] = C\\n\\n# update grid\\nself.grid = output\",\"rationale\":\"We identify the small colored shape (cells !=0 and !=8), compute its bounding box (bw,bh), detect the bottom region of 8s and compute its bounding box, calculate the scale factor as sqrt(large_count/small_count), clear the 8s, then for each small pixel, rotate it 90\u00b0 clockwise relative to the small bbox top-left, scale by factor scale, and place the colored block in the bottom region accordingly.\"}"
